{
  "id": "silverrussell-syndrome",
  "term": "Silver–Russell syndrome",
  "definition": "Silver–Russell syndrome is a rare imprinting disorder marked by slowed growth before and after birth, most often linked to loss of methylation on chromosome 11p15 or maternal uniparental disomy of chromosome 7. In psychology and learning contexts, it has been associated with reported attention and learning difficulties, although executive functioning is not clearly impaired as a defining feature.",
